    "summary": "Lovelight sandwich bookends a tight set with stellar Mason's jam",
    "blurb": "The show opens and closes with a Turn On Your Lovelight > Me & My Uncle sandwich, framing an acoustic Black Peter/ Little Sadie interlude. Alligator flows into The Other One and then into the fiery Mason's Children, all captured on a crystal‑clear soundboard.",
    "review": "Feb 28, 1970 at the Family Dog was a showcase of the Dead’s early‑70s versatility. A super‑mix soundboard captures the band in top form: Jerry weaves his signature phrasing through the opening Lovelight sandwich, while Phil’s “taught” bass sits perfectly in the crystal‑clear mix. The acoustic detour with Black Peter and Little Sadie adds a folk‑rock hush before the electric second half erupts – Alligator segues into The Other One and then launches into an unforgettable Mason's Children jam that has fans shouting, “the last Masons? Say it ain’t so Jerry.” Mickey and Bill’s drum duo is described as a “primo” four‑armed beast dancing through the transitions. Highlights also include the tight China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider pairing and a solid encore of Uncle John’s Band. With superb instrument separation and no noticeable dropouts, this recording stands out as the definitive document of the night.",
